(1) Have Reflection, to reflect its breath off, and hope that it
doesn't melee you to death in the first turn. Being fast and/or
unburdened will make sure it doesn't get a double move. (More likely,
what killed you in one turn was its breath reflecting off a wall and
hitting you twice: there is no way to get *intrinsic* acid resistance
except by polymorphing into something acid-resistant, although you can
get acid resistance by wearing certain items.)

(2) Drop a scroll of scare monster under your feet - or use a
well-known inscription - so it can't melee you in the *second* turn.
After this, it cannot injure you either with melee or breath, and you
can hit it whenever it stands next to you, or shoot it whenever it is
in line with you. Just wear it down and eventually you'll kill it.

Then turn its corpse into armour ;-)

